\begin{abstract}
This paper presents \ourmethod, a multi-agent retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) framework composed of specialized agents for subtasks such as planning, searching, reasoning, and coordination. Our system uses a self-training paradigm with reward-guided trajectory sampling to optimize inter-agent collaboration and enhance response generation. Evaluated on DataMorgana-derived datasets during the SIGIR 2025 LiveRAG competition, \ourmethod outperforms conventional RAG baselines. We further analyze competition outcomes and showcase the framework’s strengths with case studies, demonstrating its efficacy for complex, real-world RAG tasks.
\end{abstract}

