We implement a BMLP module in SWI-Prolog \cite{wielemaker:2011:tplp} called iterative extension (BMLP-IE) for the task of bottom-up evaluation of reachability in metabolic networks. Each binary vector is represented as an integer. BMLP-IE (Fig \ref{fig:bmlp_ie}b) iteratively expands the set of facts derivable from a partially grounded query $r(u, Y)$. For $\mathcal{P}$ containing $n$ constant symbols, we represent $u$ as a $1 \times n$ row vector $\mathbf{v}$. $\textbf{R}_1$ and $\textbf{R}_2$ can be multiplied with boolean vectors to turn transitions ``on'' or ``off' in the OEN to modify the network connectivity. This module gives a 170x runtime boost for this task compared to SWI-Prolog \cite{ai_boolean_2024}, showing the benefit of a special-purpose module.


